# Insecure Direct Object Reference (IDOR) on Chat Transcript Files

**Lab:** Insecure Direct Object Reference (IDOR) on chat transcripts  
**Category:** Broken Access Control / IDOR  
**Difficulty:** Apprentice  
**Platform:** PortSwigger Web Security Academy

---

# Executive Summary

The application provides users with the ability to download customer support chat transcripts. These transcripts are stored as sequentially numbered text files that can be accessed directly.

Due to the absence of authorization checks, an attacker can access chat transcripts belonging to other users. In this laboratory, a transcript contains credentials that can be used to authenticate as another user, demonstrating the impact of insecure direct object references on static resources.

